(1. MORPHOLOGICAL TYPES OF REDUPLICATION) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Tangkhul reduplication operates at both inflectional and expressive) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(levels. Type I consists of complete lexical repetition where a nominal) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(or temporal base is duplicated to signify distribution or intensity.) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(Type II consists of partial reduplication where the onset consonant is) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(copied while the nucleus vowel or coda undergoes apophonic alternation) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 9 Tf
(\(often high vowel to low vowel\).) Tj
0 -13 Td
/F1 8 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F2 10 Tf
